Zarel wrote:

>> So, Gauntlets of Stealing. Good idea or implementation nightmare?

> Good idea. You can already steal when polymorphed into a nymph or
> something, so I doubt it'd be too hard to implement.

I agree. But I think there should only be a chance of succeeding, it
shouldn't ever be 100% sure you will succeed (or else it would become
way too easy to get the Quest artifacts).

I suggest a base chance of 30% for unenchanted gloves, with a 5% bonus
for every enchantment, giving +5 gloves a 55% chance to succeed.

Next, add a 25% chance if the monster is asleep or meditating.

Failing will wake up a sleeping monster, and give it a free attack.
Monsters that were awake in the first place would get two free attacks.

If you succeed, you're presented with the monster's inventory (not
earlier, or this would be a good way to get a peek at some monster's
inventory), and you may pick the item you'd like to steal. You cannot
steal worn items, except for glasses, and trying to steal something
wielded will call for another stealing check to succeed (with the same
modifiers as for your first roll; monsters are still considered to be
asleep if they were before).

